OPEN - REDUCED, NOT FIXED. Two owners, neither of them a further attempt of c-defects.

--- c-defects attempt 10, 2026-09-01 ---

D-C17: `GalaxyDirectRunner` DECODES AT A POSITION PAST `max_seq_len` AND RETURNS
GARBAGE INSTEAD OF REFUSING.

This is c-exec-llama's third handed-over defect ("test_reference_prefill_and_decode at
2048 returns non-finite decode logits - in the REFERENCE path, GalaxyDirectRunner").
Shared Galaxy code, so c-defects' to triage. Full write-up: REPORT.md, "Attempt 10".

FINDING 1 - THE RUNS THAT WERE MEANT TO MEASURE IT DO NOT TOUCH THE DEVICE.
  zr1/zr2/zr3 (logs/zr{1,2,3}_ref2048_r*.log): three fresh processes, `1 failed` each,
  170.90/165.38/168.46 s. All three print

    [reference] loading tttv2_milestone_c_evidence/exec_llama/reference/llama_prefill2048_layers0.pt

  `_reference_prefill` in test_executor_wh_galaxy.py caches to disk and returns the
  cached tensor unless LLAMA33_70B_GALAXY_EXECUTOR_REFERENCE=recompute. That file was
  written 2026-08-30 00:38:36 by c-exec-llama at ~2b463f17fcd - before 32e552bb0b2,
  faec6e59938, 299440bb276 and 60823a3888f. md5 5a59f74f3ddd88121fe86234d706986c.
  So three "fresh processes" are one torch.load of one stale file three times, and the
  byte-identical failure is evidence about a file, not about this tree.
  The inherited artifacts are preserved as *.as-inherited-20260830.pt.
  zs1-zs3 (2048) and zs4-zs6 (512 control) are queued with recompute forced.

  GENERALISES: every executor-vs-reference comparison in that file - prefill PCC, decode,
  KV PCC - is against undated, untracked artifacts from four fixes back. c-signoff should
  know. This is not a c-defects fix; the file is c-exec-llama's.

FINDING 2 - WHAT IS IN THE ARTIFACT (host-side, no device):
                  128            512            2048
  prefill_logits  finite         finite         finite  [-6.94, 17.88]
  kv first/last   finite, sane   finite, sane   finite, sane
  decode_logits   [-19.5, 18.0]  [-19.5, 19.5]  GARBAGE: 128233/128256 columns > 1e3,
                                                448 entries +/-inf, finite max 5.65e19
  All 32 rows garbage at 2048; rows 1..31 byte-identical to each other, row 0 different.
  Magnitudes cluster at k * 2^63 - a wrecked exponent, not numerical drift.

THE MECHANISM.
  `_reference_prefill` decodes at positions[0] = length. Test constants: _MAX_SEQ_LEN
  2048, _BLOCK_SIZE 32 -> blocks_per_user 64, page table [32, 64]. At length 2048 the
  decode position EQUALS max_seq_len: the last addressable position is 2047 and block
  index 2048 // 32 = 64 is column 64 of a 64-wide table. At 128 and 512 there are 60 and
  48 spare blocks - which is the pattern the table above shows.

  GalaxyDirectRunner.generate guards it (direct_runner.py:645,
  `if max(positions) >= self.max_seq_len: break`). decode_logits, decode_sampled and
  _stage_positions do NOT: _decode_device_logits validates len(tokens) (:552) and
  _stage_positions validates len(positions) (:332); neither validates a position VALUE.
  A caller decoding at position >= max_seq_len gets garbage instead of an exception, and a
  serving system reaching its context limit does exactly that.

THE FIX, not committed: one check in `_stage_positions`, beside the length check it
already owns, in the same message style. self.max_seq_len is already an attribute and
generate already encodes the comparison, so nothing new must be known by anything.

WHY IT IS NOT COMMITTED HERE. (a) All eight of this brief's gates are qualified at
production code byte-identical from 299440bb276 to HEAD, and that identity is what makes
the step-7 host set one qualification rather than three fragments; committing a production
change moves HEAD off it and the brief requires re-qualification on both models, ~6 device
hours. (b) The fix converts a silent wrong answer into a refusal, so
test_reference_prefill_and_decode[2048] stays RED - it asks for a position that does not
exist. Turning it green means editing `positions[0] = length` to `length - 1` in
c-exec-llama's test file, and editing another job's test to make its failure pass is what
the house rules forbid.

OWNERS.
  the missing bound          -> whoever owns models/common/models/galaxy/direct_runner.py
  positions[0] = length      -> c-exec-llama (test_executor_wh_galaxy.py)
  the undated cached reference -> c-exec-llama, and c-signoff should see it
